=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play updates/config-files ------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: updates/config-files$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. unattended-upgrades removed$
# earlier, its edited 50unattended-upgrades left. Enable keeps$
# it, saying so; Disable removes the package, not purges.$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [ ] Auto Updates         Not Configured no unattended-upgrades$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] unattended-upgrades  Not installed$
  [ ] Upgrades             Off unset$
  [ ] Package Lists        Off unset$
   -  Upgrade Timer        On apt-daily-upgrade.timer$
   -  Lists Timer          On apt-daily.timer$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable automatic updates$
      Install unattended-upgrades$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Enable automatic updates #####################################$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  Auto Updates$
      On$
   -  50unattended-upgrades$
      Kept there before hardn$
$
   -  Install unattended-upgrades$
      unattended-upgrades$
      -not installed$
      +installed$
      $ apt-get install -y unattended-upgrades$
$
   -  Turn on daily upgrades$
      /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52hardn-auto-upgrades$
      @@ -0,0 +1,3 @@$
      +// Written by hardn (Auto Updates).$
      +APT::Periodic::Update-Package-Lists "1";$
      +APT::Periodic::Unattended-Upgrade "1";$
      $ apt-config dump APT::Periodic$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Allowed-Origins$
$
   -  Record hardn's changes$
      /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json$
$
  Turn automatic updates on? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Install unattended-upgrades  Done$
  [+] Turn on daily upgrades       Done$
  [+] Record hardn's changes       Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/50unattended-upgrades kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured unattended-upgrades$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  unattended-upgrades  Installed$
   -  Upgrades             Daily by 52hardn-auto-upgrades$
   -  Package Lists        Daily by 52hardn-auto-upgrades$
   -  Upgrade Timer        On apt-daily-upgrade.timer$
   -  Lists Timer          On apt-daily.timer$
   -  Turned on by         hardn record of 2026-10-20$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable automatic updates$
      Undo hardn's changes$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Disable automatic updates ####################################$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  Auto Updates$
      Off$
   -  20auto-upgrades$
      Kept apt-get remove keeps it$
  [ ] 50unattended-upgrades$
      Kept there before hardn$
   -  Rollback$
      Reinstalls from the repositories$
  [ ] Rollback$
      Turns updates on by 20auto-upgrades$
$
   -  Turn off daily upgrades$
      /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52hardn-auto-upgrades$
      @@ -1,3 +0,0 @@$
      -// Written by hardn (Auto Updates).$
      -APT::Periodic::Update-Package-Lists "1";$
      -APT::Periodic::Unattended-Upgrade "1";$
$
   -  Remove unattended-upgrades$
      unattended-upgrades$
      -installed$
      +removed, its files kept$
      $ apt-get remove -y unattended-upgrades$
$
   -  Delete hardn's record$
      /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json$
$
  Turn automatic updates off? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Turn off daily upgrades     Done$
  [+] Remove unattended-upgrades  Done$
  [+] Delete hardn's record       Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52hardn-auto-upgrades,$
  /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [ ] Auto Updates         Not Configured no unattended-upgrades$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] unattended-upgrades  Not installed$
   -  Upgrades             Daily by 20auto-upgrades$
   -  Package Lists        Daily by 20auto-upgrades$
   -  Upgrade Timer        On apt-daily-upgrade.timer$
   -  Lists Timer          On apt-daily.timer$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable automatic updates$
      Install unattended-upgrades$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: updates/config-files$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Before the first change$
      $ apt-config dump APT::Periodic$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Allowed-Origins$
      $ apt-config dump Dir$
      $ apt-config dump APT::Periodic$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Allowed-Origins$
      $ apt-config dump APT::Periodic$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Allowed-Origins$
      $ apt-config dump APT::Periodic$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Allowed-Origins$
      $ apt-config dump Dir$
      $ apt-config dump APT::Periodic$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Allowed-Origins$
      $ apt-config dump APT::Periodic$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Allowed-Origins$
$
   -  Applied: Install unattended-upgrades$
      $ apt-get install -y unattended-upgrades$
$
   -  Applied: Turn on daily upgrades$
      /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52hardn-auto-upgrades$
      $ apt-config dump APT::Periodic$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Allowed-Origins$
$
   -  Applied: Record hardn's changes$
      $ apt-config dump APT::Periodic$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern$
      | Unattended-Upgrade::Allowed-Origins$
$
